{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Next Step"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Media Kit"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "  Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le15ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reason Clauses: Due to, because of, owing to <br/>Result Clauses: So ... that"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to introduce a reason for a particular situation, you can use these prepositions at the beginning of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">because of </span></span>before a noun or a noun phrase."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We won't be able to make it <span class=\"strong\">because of the weather</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">Due to</span></span> and <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">owing to</span></span> also mean <span class=\"italic\">because of</span>. They sound a little more formal, and are therefore more common in professional English rather than conversational."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">She was unable to attend the meeting <span class=\"strong\">due to a previous engagement</span>.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We have less money to spend <span class=\"strong\">owing to the budget cuts</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to link a cause with a result, you can use <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">so ... that</span></span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The bus was <span class=\"strong\">so </span>hot <span class=\"strong\">that </span>I felt sick the whole way!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You normally use an adjective or adverb after so. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">It all happened so <span class=\"strong\">quickly </span>that I never had a chance to fully absorb what was going on.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In formal English, you can put <span class=\"italic\">So ... that</span> at the beginning of the sentence and put the verb before the object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">So hot was the bus that</span> I felt sick the whole way.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It has to be done quickly due to the looming release date next week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was so interesting that I'd like to focus on writing media kits. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sometimes it's hard to stand out in this industry, owing to the volume of competition."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The small publishers sometimes get overlooked because of the ubiquity of the large ones."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Testimonials are so influential that I'd like to try to get five in our media kit. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Creating a Media Kit"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "What is a media kit?<br/>A package of information assembled by a company to provide basic information about itself to reporters."}, {"type": "text", "content": "How do you create a media kit? <br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>First you write an introduction of who you are, in this case the author and the title of the book. </li><li>Next you can include a mission or manifesto to differentiate your business or product from the competition and explaining what the business stands for.</li><li>Next I put in some factual information about the product, our book.</li><li>I added in a couple illustrations so people can see how beautiful they are.</li><li>Next you should put in some testimonials or quotes from people saying how great they think the product is.</li><li>The last section is the price list and contact information for bookstores, libraries or schools that want to order the book from the publisher.</li><li>It needs to be in PDF form, so converting to PDF is the last step.</li>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "looming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "about to \u200bhappen \u200bsoon and \u200bcausing \u200bworry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It has to be done quickly due to the looming release date next week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about customer relations."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "media kit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "A package of information assembled by a company to provide basic information about itself to reporters."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  How are you coming along with the media kit for the book?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "manifesto"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a public declaration of policy and aims"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "con